In the upper-right corner of any page on GitHub, click your profile picture, then click  Settings.

In the "Access" section of the sidebar, click  Password and authentication.

In the "Two-factor authentication" section of the page, click Enable two-factor authentication.

Complete the CAPTCHA challenge, which helps protect against spam and abuse.

Under "Verify account", select your country code and type your mobile phone number,
including the area code. When your information is correct, click Send authentication code.

You'll receive a text message with a security code. On GitHub,
type the code into the field under "Verify the code sent to your phone" and click Continue.

If you need to edit the phone number you entered, you'll need to complete another CAPTCHA challenge.
